.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pons 1  "pons 0.1.0-dev.1"
.SH NAME
pons \- Spot rookie mistakes beyond successful compilation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpons\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pons scans source and repository documents without executing project code. Findings are evidence\-labelled suggestions. Exit codes: 0 completed below the chosen failure threshold, 1 threshold reached, 2 invalid input or incomplete scan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pons\-scan(1)
Scan a file or tree. Does not execute scanned code or external plug\-ins
.TP
pons\-catalogue(1)
Print the built\-in rule catalogue (generated from the registry)
.TP
pons\-man(1)
Generate a man page from the same command model as \-\-help
.TP
pons\-doctor(1)
Show installed optional tools without claiming they are tested
.TP
pons\-challenge(1)
Ask the separately installed Invariant Path to examine a document\*(Aqs claims. Produces JSON; does not persist or accept annotations
.TP
pons\-extract(1)
Convert a document/image to text using a named optional local tool
.TP
pons\-spell(1)
List dictionary misses using aspell or hunspell; no automatic rewrites
.TP
pons\-search(1)
Approximate text search via the installed agrep executable
.TP
pons\-trace(1)
Check an explicit ordered JSON event trace against a supplied TOML contract. Does not infer events or control flow from source code
.TP
pons\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0\-dev.1
